        <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <details class="ar-faq-item" open><summary><h3>Where are most hoodies manufactured?</h3></summary><p>The majority of the world's hoodies are manufactured in Asia, led by China, Vietnam, Bangladesh, and India. China handles the widest range of order sizes and decoration types, while Vietnam and Bangladesh dominate high-volume basic fleece production. Turkey and Portugal serve European brands seeking faster delivery and high-end construction</p></details>

          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>Is it cheaper to manufacture hoodies in China or Bangladesh?</h3></summary><p>Bangladesh is generally cheaper for large-volume basic hoodies, with unit costs running meaningfully below comparable Chinese production once you pass roughly 1,000 pieces per color. China becomes more cost-effective for smaller runs, complex decoration, and multi-SKU orders, where its supply-chain flexibility reduces waste and rework</p></details>

          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>What is the minimum order quantity for custom hoodies?</h3></summary><p>MOQ varies by country and fabric. China commonly accepts 100–500 pieces per color on stock fabrics, Portugal and Turkey sit around 150–1,000 pieces, and Bangladesh typically starts at 1,000–3,000 pieces. Custom-dyed fabric raises the minimum almost everywhere, because the dyehouse sets its own batch size</p></details>

          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>Which country is best for small-batch hoodie production?</h3></summary><p>China, Portugal, and Turkey are the strongest options for small-batch hoodie production. China offers the widest fabric and decoration range at low MOQs, Portugal delivers high-end construction on 150–500 piece runs, and Turkey balances quality with speed for European brands</p></details>

          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>How long does hoodie manufacturing take?</h3></summary><p>Sampling typically takes 7–25 days depending on country and complexity. Bulk production runs 25–90 days, with China and Turkey at the faster end and Bangladesh at the slower end. Add 10–20 days for custom dyeing and 25–35 days for ocean freight. Air freight cuts transit to about a week but raises cost sharply</p></details>

          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>Do hoodie manufacturers offer OEM and ODM services?</h3></summary><p>Most established hoodie manufacturers offer both. OEM means the factory produces to your designs and tech packs. ODM means it supplies existing designs you adapt with your own branding. OEM gives you more control and differentiation, while ODM gets you to market faster and cheaper</p></details>

          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>What certifications should I look for in a hoodie factory?</h3></summary><p>Look for social-compliance audits such as WRAP or BSCI, quality-management certification such as ISO 9001, and chemical or environmental certification such as OEKO-TEX where your category requires it. Requirements depend on your target retailers, so confirm which frameworks they accept before you select a factory</p></details>

          <details class="ar-faq-item"><summary><h3>Can I get hoodie samples before placing a bulk order?</h3></summary><p>Yes, and you should. Reputable factories provide fit samples, lab dips, and pre-production samples, usually for a fee that is often credited against the bulk order. Always approve a pre-production sample before mass production begins</p></details>

